  "worked_solution": "The formulae for the derivatives of $arctan$ and $arcsec$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arctanx) & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(arcsec({x}^{2}))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(arcsec({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(arcsec({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(arcsec({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{arcsec}^{2}({x}^{2}))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
